{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786480183,"nonce":"TMSufQ44XaNasTLjAKMbH3kQyt0=","title":"**What is wrong.** Six skipped `TestBUG_*` tests across five packages all pin the same root cause: handlers refuse an unknown query parameter with `400 unknown_parameter` exactly as SPEC §E.3 requires, and `api/openapi/openapi.yaml` declares no `400` for the operation. A generated client therefore has no schema for a response its own server will send the first time a proxy or a browser appends a parameter to a URL — and the contract-driven assertion cannot even be written, because `schema.AssertProblem` fails at the LOOKUP rather than at the validation.","message":"**In every case the CONTRACT is what is wrong**, not the handler. The refusal is correct and specified; the response list simply never gained the `BadRequest` entry that sibling operations already carry.\n\n**The pins.**\n\n| Package | Test | Operations |\n|---|---|---|\n| `internal/channels/api` | `TestBUG_UnknownQueryParameterOnAnIdAddressedChannelEndpointIsAnUndeclared400` | id-addressed channel reads |\n| `internal/drill/api` | `TestBUG_TheIdAddressedDrillRoutesCanAnswerAnUndeclared400` | id-addressed drill reads |\n| `internal/enrichment/api` | `TestBUG_AnUnknownQueryParameterIsRefusedWithAStatusTheContractDoesNotDeclare` | enricher reads |\n| `internal/grouping/api` | `TestBUG_ADetailReadCanAnswerAnUndeclared400` | `getAlertGroup` |\n| `internal/rules/api` | `TestBUG_AnUnknownQueryParameterIsRefusedWithAStatusTheContractNeverDeclares` | `getRuleSnapshot`, `getOccurrenceRule`, `getAlertRuleHistory` |\n\n**A seventh, adjacent and NOT the same fix.** `TestBUG_ListDeliveryDrillsRefusesAMissingSourceIDWithAnUndeclaredStatus` in `internal/drill/api` is the mirror image: here the SERVER is wrong. `listDeliveryDrills` answers **422** for a missing required query parameter while declaring no 422 at all, and the contract states a 422 always carries `violations[]` — this one does not. A missing required QUERY parameter is the `400 malformed_request` family `httpx.NewParams` already uses; 422 is for a body that parsed and is semantically invalid. Fix the handler, not the contract.\n\n**Why it matters.** These are not theoretical. `unknown_parameter` fires on the most ordinary input there is — a tracking parameter, a stale bookmark, a client that appends `?_=timestamp`. Every one of these operations can hand a generated client a status it has no branch for, on a first call.\n\n**Done when.** Each operation declares `'400': $ref: '#/components/responses/BadRequest'`; `listDeliveryDrills` answers 400 rather than 422 for a missing `source_id`; the generated client and validators are regenerated (G3/G4); and all six pins are unskipped.","files":null}]}